{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSbnoVR947ZEPKdwoQiE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Repository Summary for Analysis\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions active orders to `CANCELLED` status, cancelling their `CREATED` shipments, with idempotent semantics and proper handling of blocked states.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11-16): No status field; created via OrderController:31\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27): Stores in ConcurrentHashMap, provides save/findById\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-14): Already has ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): No method to find shipments by orderId\n- Error handling (ApiExceptions.kt:18-24): ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n- Tests (OrderControllerTest.kt:22-75): Verify both status code and error response shape\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Errors thrown as ApiException subclasses, handled by GlobalExceptionHandler to produce ApiError envelope\n2. Error codes are enum values (ErrorCode.java:31-37)\n3. Repositories use in-memory ConcurrentHashMap\n4. Controllers inject repositories and throw exceptions\n5. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for error shape\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — add status field\n2. OrderController.kt — add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — add method to find by orderId\n4. ApiError.kt — add error codes for cancel scenarios\n5. OrderControllerTest.kt — add tests for cancel behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Changing Order breaks existing test assertions unless they accommodate new field\n2. All-or-nothing semantics with CONFIRMED shipments requires validation before state change\n3. Idempotency (succeed on already-CANCELLED) must not confuse with actual errors\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket is explicit about all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class. Create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws ConflictException if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - Changes order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments (all-or-nothing)\n   - Returns the updated order\n   - Succeeds silently if order is already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt** — Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for creating shipment on cancelled order) and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for blocking cancel).\n\n5. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Cancel active order with no shipments\n   - Cancel active order with CREATED shipments (should cancel them)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment (409, unchanged)\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order (succeeds, idempotent)\n   - Cancel non-existent order (404)\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** — Modify create endpoint to reject if order is CANCELLED (409 with ORDER_CANCELLED).\n\n**Alternative rejected:** Inject OrderRepository into ShipmentController to check order status. Rejected because ShipmentController should depend on ShipmentRepository only; instead, the cancel operation handles shipments by keeping them in CREATED state for cancellation, and when creating a new shipment, we can inject and check the order. Actually, this means ShipmentController needs access to OrderRepository. This is the correct design — shipment creation validates the order exists and is not cancelled.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel active order (no shipments):**\n   - GET order by orderId → found, status=ACTIVE\n   - Query shipments by orderId → empty list\n   - UPDATE order status to CANCELLED\n   - Return updated order with status=CANCELLED\n\n2. **Cancel active order (CREATED shipments):**\n   - GET order by orderId → found, status=ACTIVE\n   - Query shipments by orderId → found (status=CREATED)\n   - Validate no CONFIRMED shipments → pass\n   - UPDATE order status to CANCELLED\n   - UPDATE all CREATED shipments status to CANCELLED\n   - Return updated order with status=CANCELLED\n\n3. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - GET order by orderId → found, status=ACTIVE\n   - Query shipments by orderId → found (status=CONFIRMED)\n   - Validate no CONFIRMED shipments → fail\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n   - Nothing changes (all-or-nothing)\n\n4. **Cancel already-cancelled order:**\n   - GET order by orderId → found, status=CANCELLED\n   - Query shipments by orderId → may have shipments\n   - Return order as-is (idempotent success)\n\n5. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - GET order by orderId → not found\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n6. **Create shipment for cancelled order:**\n   - GET order by orderId → found, status=CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `cancel_active_order_with_no_shipments` — Verify order transitions to CANCELLED\n2. `cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments` — Verify shipments transition to CANCELLED\n3. `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409` — Verify ConflictException, no state change\n4. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` — Verify idempotent (no error, returns CANCELLED order)\n5. `cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404` — Verify ResourceNotFoundException\n6. `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` — Verify ORDER_CANCELLED error\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_t